course: dictionary
lesson: 8953
title: Silverfish and damp places
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one. «Silverfish nibble old books» is about an insect, because nibbling books is what a tiny bug does, not a fish. The words around the word are its context, and they leave clues.
explain: Silverfish is a noun. One is «a silverfish» and more than one is «silverfish». Its name is a clue too: it is silver, and it wriggles like a fish. But it is an insect with no wings, not a fish.
explain: Look at the setting. «Your home is a small wild world: spiders hunt in the corners, silverfish nibble old books...» The words corners, old books and home tell you where silverfish live: somewhere quiet, dark and damp.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If a silverfish is a small silver insect with no wings, does «silverfish eat starch» still make sense? Yes, so you have understood it.
fact: A silverfish is a small, shiny, silver-grey insect with no wings.
fact: Silverfish wriggle like fish and live in damp corners of houses.
fact: «Silverfish» can also be a name for some small silvery fish, but this meaning is rare.
fact: Silverfish eat starch, such as the stuff in flour and pasta, as well as glue, paper and crumbs.
fact: Silverfish like damp, dark places and can live a year without food.
exercise: «Silverfish nibble old books.» What kind of place might silverfish be found in? | *A damp, dark corner | A sunny field of flowers | A bright, busy playground | A hot, dry desert
exercise: What is a silverfish? | A fish that lives in the sea | *A small, silver-grey insect with no wings | A spider with eight long legs | A large bird that can fly high
exercise: «Silverfish are wingless insects with three long tails.» Find and copy one word that tells you silverfish have no wings. | three | tails | insects | *wingless
test: «Silverfish eat starch, glue, paper and crumbs.» What do silverfish eat? | Grass and leaves from the garden | Honey and fresh flowers | *Starch, glue, paper and crumbs | Only fish and worms
test: Ella says silverfish must be fish because of their name. What is the best answer? | *They are insects, though their name and wriggle are like a fish | They are fish, because the word silver is only used for fish | They are plants that grow under sinks | They are birds that swim in damp corners
exam: «Silverfish can live a year without food.» What does this tell you about silverfish? | They need food every hour to stay alive | *They can survive a long time without eating | They never sleep or move | They can only live in the sea
